        "y": 24.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 406.1,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Education: debates and issues"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.7,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 240.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Opportunity and equality"
      },
      {
        "y": 99,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 508,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "All education systems may ultimately be judged in terms of equality of opportunity1. This is often"
      },
      {
        "y": 111,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 496,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "referred to in the debates over selective2 versus comprehensive3 schooling4. The main issue is"
      },
      {
        "y": 123,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 507.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "whether everyone has the same opportunities for educational achievement or whether elitism5 of"
      },
      {
        "y": 135,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 297.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "one sort or another is inherent in6 the system."
      },
      {
        "y": 149.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 474.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "League tables7 for schools and colleges may actually help unintentionally to perpetuate8"
      },
      {
        "y": 162.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 495.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "inequalities, while claiming to promote the raising of standards. Inevitably, league tables divide"
      },
      {
        "y": 173.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 496.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "educational institutions into good and bad, success and failure, resulting in a two-tier system9,"
      },
      {
        "y": 185.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 478.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "or at least that is how the public perceives10 it. The ability of better-off11 parents and well-"
      },
      {
        "y": 197.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 498.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "endowed12 schools to push children towards the institutions at the top of the league may, in the"
      },
      {
        "y": 209.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 500.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "long term, have the effect of depressing13 opportunity for the less well-off14 or for children from"
      },
      {
        "y": 221.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 417.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "home environments that do not provide the push and motivation to excel15."
      },
      {
        "y": 237.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 501.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Financial support of different kinds can help to make educational opportunity more equal. There"
      },
      {
        "y": 248.6,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 507.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "are, for example, scholarships16 or bursaries17 that make it possible for less privileged youngsters"
      },
      {
        "y": 260.6,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 496.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "to afford tertiary18 education. Student loans19 allow undergraduates20 to pay for their tuition"
      },
      {
        "y": 272.6,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 480.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "fees21 and living expenses while they are studying. But few would claim that real equality of"
      },
      {
        "y": 285.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 238.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "opportunity has been achieved."
      },
      {
        "y": 310.2,
        "x0": 102.3,
        "x1": 365.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 when everyone has the same chances 11 richer"
