        "x1": 179.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "are necessary."
      },
      {
        "y": 207.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 313.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 Inequality is built into the education system."
      },
      {
        "y": 219.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 452.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 Giving access only to privileged groups is bad for the country in the long term."
      },
      {
        "y": 231.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 519.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 Education where everyone gets into the same type of school without exams is a basic political"
      },
      {
        "y": 243.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 227.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "ideal in many countries."
      },
      {
        "y": 255.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 535.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 A system where there are two levels of schools reduces the opportunities for children from poorer"
      },
      {
        "y": 267.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 323.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "families and favours those from richer families."
      },
      {
        "y": 279.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 538.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 Some private schools have lots of wealth and receive gifts of money, and this means they can have"
      },
      {
        "y": 291.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 198,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "better resources."
      },
      {
        "y": 303.3,
